to others.  I like your indirect object formulation, though the use of
'covet' doesn't grab me since I associate more negatives with that word
(the result of childhood Sunday School?).  In fact, when I wrote my example
sentence, I first wrote "I envy you your car, Phred", and then changed
it to what I posted because I decided what I first wrote wasn't good
English.  So maybe I'll go with that, and hope the meaning is clearer.
